  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The electric potential at the surface of an atomic nucleus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>)</mo></math> of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. What is the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math>?</p><p>(Charge of proton <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>)</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The electric potential at the surface of an atomic nucleus can be written as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>·</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>From equation (1), it follows that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>V</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup><mo>×</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></msup><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
